  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Citizen-State Relations in Central Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promote inclusive dialogue at the regional level leads to a common understanding on key security issues, the identification of conflict sensitive responses and the reinforcement of women partcipation in the peace process</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Setting and run up of women only regional forum sothat to promote women participation in the decision  making and their rigths.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will target communities&#x2019; women associations, Security and Defense Forces&#x2019; representatives, civil society actors and regional authorities as direct beneficiaries in Segou and Mopti. Regional target groups will be drawn from regional directorate, traditional authorities, the SDF, law enforcement representatives, and other members of the target communities at regional level and the member of the existing local forum.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will promote a common understanding of the forums members on key security issues, the identification of conflict-sensitive responses  at the regional level and contribute to reducing the threat from criminality, political and extremist violence in the regions of Segou and Mopti in Mali.</narrative>
  </description>
